; RT31 / PT31 (#723): the reading checks that the edge loops are closed with
; isClosed and the tolerance rule of the document being read (card, point 2;
; DECISIONI.md, 2026-11-16). Three handwritten files with the same two SOLID
; hatches, in millimetres ($INSUNITS 4), without $INSUNITS (0, the
; millimetre rule) and in metres ($INSUNITS 6, tolerance 1e-9):
; 20 lines 0,0->10,0, 10,0->10,8, 10,8->0,8, 0,8->0.0000005,0: the gap
;    between the last edge and the first is 5e-7;
; 21 the same square at x 20..30 with the last line ending in 20,1: a gap of
;    1, open in every unit.
; Values from the card; not an oracle case (ezdxf does not check closure).
M = DXF file=millimetri.dxf
N = DXF file=senza-unita.dxf
K = DXF file=metri.dxf
? units M -> 4
? units N -> 0
? units K -> 6
; PT31 makes HATCH a handled entity: until then every HATCH is unhandled.
; cambia con #723
? count M -> HATCH 1
? unhandled M -> HATCH 1
? entity M 20 -> HATCH pattern="SOLID" solid=yes angle=0 scale=1 islands=normal loop=external+edges line=0,0;10,0 line=10,0;10,8 line=10,8;0,8 line=0,8;0.0000005,0 seed=1,1
? entity M 21 -> unhandled HATCH
? count N -> HATCH 1
? unhandled N -> HATCH 1
? entity N 20 -> HATCH pattern="SOLID" solid=yes angle=0 scale=1 islands=normal loop=external+edges line=0,0;10,0 line=10,0;10,8 line=10,8;0,8 line=0,8;0.0000005,0 seed=1,1
? entity N 21 -> unhandled HATCH
? count K -> none
? unhandled K -> HATCH 2
? entity K 20 -> unhandled HATCH
? entity K 21 -> unhandled HATCH
; Handled or raw, each file is rewritten unchanged (ADR 0018, point 6).
? roundtrip M -> identical
? roundtrip N -> identical
? roundtrip K -> identical
